    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by three elite plays: **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.01), **Yordan Alvarez** (76.23), and **Christian Yelich** (75.84). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns the top spot in our rankings due to a premier matchup against Teng, benefiting from a favorable platoon split (+14%) and the high-leverage leadoff role. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher test against Rea, his elite xwOBA of .419 sustains his value despite a modest SP matchup. **Christian Yelich** rounds out our core, leveraging a significant boost from an assumed order position and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Roki Sasaki. We are also closely monitoring **Trea Turner** (71.06); though wind blowing in presents a slight drag, the combination of his leadoff positioning and a favorable matchup against a slower-delivering pitcher\u2014who historically offers high stolen base potential\u2014keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nOur bench strategy was dictated largely by external factors and injury management. The most notable absences include **Junior Caminero** and **Colt Keith**, both of whom were scratched due to rainouts, effectively removing them from consideration despite strong underlying profiles. Among players who were healthy but missed the cut, **Chase Meidroth** and **Hyeseong Kim** represent our \"marginal\" tier; they remain on the periphery because their projected output fails to offset the potential risk of negative platoon adjustments or sub-optimal lineup placement. We remain cautious with **Gary Sanchez**, whose score of 56.53 reflects a high reliance on the matchup against Roki Sasaki; if he is not confirmed in the #6 hole, his utility will drop, and we will look to rotate in depth pieces like **Josh Smith** or **Lars Nootbaar** if late-breaking lineup data suggests a more favorable entry point. Managing our remaining bench assets\u2014**Zac Veen**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Luis Pena**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Kazuma Okamoto**\u2014will be the priority as we navigate the weekend to ensure we optimize our limited game caps while prioritizing the scarcity of stolen bases.",
